    "reason": {
     "type": "string",
     "pattern": "\\S",
     "description": "Why this case applies, naming the words that decide it."
    },
    "periods": {
     "anyOf": [
      {
       "type": "null"
      },
      {
       "type": "array",
       "items": {
        "type": "string"
       }
      }
     ],
     "description": "The two years, for one_quantity_two_periods only; null for every other case."
    }
   }
  }
 ],
 "description": "Why no judged question is written, as one case of this closed set, or null: no_main: the topic has no main figure or event (none, or several with none the main one); not_checkable_on_a_date: nothing in it can be checked on a date (for an event: no date given and no period named, unless it is a pending regulatory decision, which is due at the company's current fiscal year-end); quarter_or_half_year: a company's figure for a quarter or a half-year; not_one_year_period: a figure for a period that is not one fiscal or calendar year, such as a survey's rolling twelve months, with no publication day in the topic or the item; year_ended: a figure for a year that has already ended on the item's day; beyond_next_year: a figure for a year beyond next year (unless the topic's opens_as is binding_obligation); another_company_or_uncovered_matter: the question belongs to another company or to a matter no listed theme covers (name it); one_quantity_two_periods: the topic asks the value of one quantity for each of two years, this year and next, and neither year is named only as a base or a comparison (this case, not no_main): name the two years in periods, written as a figure's year is written (2026, or FY2027); each year is then asked as its own question. Exactly one of no_ladder and ladder is null (checked by code)."
}

## The yearly re-ask's added line

Write the question for {year} only: this topic is split by year, and where the instructions above differ, this line prevails. The value for {other} is asked as its own question, so the two-year decline case does not apply here and that value alone is not listed in not_judged. List every other part as before; where a part joins the {other} value with another limit, a condition or a comparison, list that limit, condition or comparison.

